It is a timing artifact. It happens when you are 
affected by two delayed causes of death at once. 
There is a variable, delayed_killer, that stores 
the ultimate cause of death for later, which gets
overwritten if the player contracts a second 
delayed cause of death before expiring. 

For example, eating a cockatrice egg will cause 
you to start stiffening. Should you die of the 
stiffening, the ultimate cause of death will be
eating that egg, but the proximate cause will 
just be turning to stone. Therefore, the game 
must store the string "cockatrice egg" in 
delayed_killer, so that it still knows what 
the ultimate cause of your death was 5 turns 
later when the stiffening timer runs out and 
you finally turn to stone.

Continuing the example, if you get were to be
hit by a green slime before the stiffening 
process is complete, the game would replace 
the current value of delayed_killer 
("cockatrice egg") with a new value ("green 
slime"). However, just getting hit by a 
green slime does nothing to cure stiffening. 
Therefore, you would still turn to stone at 
the end of the stiffening process, and the 
cause of death would read: "petrified by a 
green slime."

Translating the weird death messages, then:
> >>>       9 turned to slime by a cockatrice egg

As rpresser found, this one means they ate a 
cockatrice egg while dieing of sliming.

> >>>       6 turned to slime by a scroll of genocide

This one is a bit sneakier. Only delayed causes 
of death trigger the bug, so to get this message
you have to be polymorphed to another form, 
become afflicted by sliming, and then wipe out 
your own original species (so that you get the 
"You feel dead inside" message).

> >>>       1 petrified by genocidal confusion

Likewise, this guy or gal was polymorphed into 
another species, became afflicted with stiffening,
and then wiped out their original species with
confused genocide.

